### Implementation notes

- `@rat-stack/capability/sandbox` exports only the Worker-safe service contract; the root barrel keeps the Node subprocess implementation for unchanged CLI behavior.
- `@rat-stack/capability/code-mode`, `/toolkit`, `/define`, and `/http-api` keep the Worker bundle off the Node subprocess barrel.
- `toHttpApi` now accepts an optional path prefix so handler registration and generated OpenAPI agree on `/api/*`.
- Worker Loader receives generated ES modules, not `eval` or `new Function`; each call gets a fresh isolate, `globalOutbound: null`, CPU/subrequest limits, cooperative and host timeouts, narrow RPC, JSON round-tripping, and eager disposal.
- The `cloudflare:workers` runtime import stays lazy. A static import makes Alchemy's Node Stack loader reject the special `cloudflare:` URL before bundling.
- The generator reads every `skills/*/SKILL.md` and all seven law sources at build time. Request handling never reads the filesystem.
- `apps/mischief/public/{favicon-32.png,icon-512.png,og.png}` were preserved untouched. The shipped `domain` and `assets` Worker properties were retained.
- No Cloudflare authentication, deployment, commit, or production mutation occurred.
